A||N||2||Seanh||My steering rack and pinion will not come off!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||06-17-2001||04:38 AM||||Its all unbolted, but it will not come off from the steering linkage. Its really pissing me off, Iv been yanking as hard as I can for the past 4 hours with no progress. Iv also pryed with a pry bar, to no avail. What the hell do I do?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-17-2001||08:16 AM||||You have taken the 11mm lock bolt out of the steering shaft, right? If you have rotate the wheel to a point that you can drive a small wedge between the clamping surfaces so it will come loose.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||06-17-2001||11:18 AM||||Yeah, I removed the screw, but never drove a wedge into the clamp. I was ready to remove it last night at about 1am and gave up at 4am, we pulled, hammered, yanked, pried, kicked, and jerked the hell outta that thing and it just wouldn't come off. We out the this morning after reading your post, drive a screw driver into the clamp and damn rack fell right out onto the floor. Dang I love this forum! Thanks||||reg||1
